### Version 0.9.4 (2026-11-16)

Form controls on one spec, Escape ownership, and component behavior fixed alongside the docs alignment.

- **New components**: none
- **Main updated components**: form, text, image-preview, image-generation, input, textarea, number-input, select, flat-select, date-picker, cascader, tag-input, tree-select, sensitive-input, base-anchor, dialog, modal, drawer, radio, miko, offline-state, working-indicator, tool-call-card, grid-layout, motion-control, skeleton, toast, toast-panel, text-morph, text-transformer
- **Key features**:
  - `TxFormItem` gains `hint`: field help sits behind a `?` beside the label and opens on hover or keyboard focus.
  - `TxText` gains `scroll="loop"` and `loopEdge` edge effects (`gap`, `clip`, `fade`, `wrap`).
  - `TxImagePreview` gains `loadingEffect` and a `loading` slot: while loading it shows a TxImageGeneration preset, a skeleton, or nothing.
  - Form controls follow `TxInput`: number input, date field, flat select and multi select are 32px tall, corners are 12px, and edges are inset rings that keep the box size.
  - An open anchored layer handles Escape first, so the surrounding `TxModal` / `TxDrawer` stays open; Escape from a form field no longer closes the dialog.
  - `TxMiko` loads each state lazily; its default color is the lighter `#9726D9`.
  - `TxOfflineState` forwards `primary` / `secondary`; `TxWorkingIndicator` and `TxToolCallCard` stop ticking while off screen.
  - Fixes: the `TxRadioGroup` indicator re-measures when the group resizes, `TxSensitiveInput` stays revealed while focus moves to its copy button, `TxBlowDialog` clears the page zoom on unmount, and skeletons and collapsed toasts are hidden from screen readers.

### Version 0.9.3 (2026-11-03)

Touch surfaces, the Miko desktop companion, text overflow, and custom emoji packs.

- **New components**: touch-surface, miko, text
- **Main updated components**: chain-of-thought, glass-surface, stream-markdown, icon-picker, markdown-editor, icon
- **Key features**:
  - New `TxText`: the ellipsis can sit at the start, middle or end of overflowing text (`overflow`); `scroll="auto"` loops the text back and forth, and `scroll="hover"` truncates at rest and slides the rest in on hover. On touch, `hover` becomes a tap toggle, and both scroll modes stop under reduced motion.
  - New `TxTouchSurface` and `useLiquidTouch`: a surface that behaves like a drop of liquid glass under a hovering or pressing pointer.
  - New `TxMiko`, the desktop companion cat.
  - `TxIconPicker` and `TxMarkdownEditor` accept `emojiPacks`: the picker stores a picked emoji as a `url:` identifier, and the editor inserts `:name:` and renders it as an image; shortcodes are 2–40 characters.
  - `TxGlassSurface` gains `engine="lens"` (the default stays `classic`), and `useLiquidDrag` is new.
  - `TxChainOfThought` streams its thinking text at a steady pace.
  - Fixes the `TxStreamMarkdown` table copy-as-CSV button, which a sticky header used to half-cover.

### Version 0.9.2 (2026-10-27)

A rewritten form system, a full-window image preview, and solid drawer surfaces by default.

- **New components**: drawer-form, image-preview, modal-form, steps-form
- **Main updated components**: attachment-tray, base-surface, charts, command-palette, dialog, drawer, flip-overlay, form, image-gallery, input, modal, motion-transition, number-input, select, sensitive-input, stream-markdown, switch, textarea
- **Key features**:
  - `TxForm` and `TxFormItem` are rewritten. `layout` moves labels beside or above fields by the form's own width; rules gain `type`, `min` / `max`, length and `pattern`; `level: 'warning'` reports without blocking submit, and `deps` revalidates a field when the fields it depends on change. Controls inside a form item pick up its label, required state, error and readonly state automatically.
  - `TxForm` gains drafts (`persist`), autosave (`autosave`) and `readonly`: drafts are keyed by the form's `id`, survive a reload or a closed tab, and are dropped after a successful submit or `reset()`.
  - New `TxModalForm` and `TxDrawerForm` edit a record in a dialog or a drawer, always on a copy of `initialValues`, and close only after a successful submit. New `TxStepsForm` and `TxFormStep` split one form across steps: it takes `v-model`, validates each step before moving on, and submits the whole form at the end.
  - New `TxImagePreview`: wheel and pinch zoom, pan with momentum once zoomed, horizontal swipe to page while unzoomed, drag up or down to close, and a flight from the thumbnail. `TxImageGallery` and `TxAttachmentTray` route through it and load it the first time it is needed.
  - `TxDrawer` panels use a solid surface by default (`surface` defaults to `pure`), so the page behind no longer shows through; pass `surface="refraction"` for the glass look.
  - Chart labels can follow the interface language: `TxTimeseriesChart` and `TxSankeyChart` gain `labels` entries, `TxMonoChart` gains `formatX`.
  - One Tab-cycle rule across dialogs: only visible, tabbable controls are stops, skipping hidden ones, `inert` subtrees and `tabindex="-1"`; `TxDrawer` moves focus into the panel when it opens.
  - dompurify is upgraded past its critical and high advisories.

### Version 0.9.1 (2026-10-21)

Fixes the refraction-surface jank that 0.9.0 brought to large panels.

- **New components**: None.
- **Main updated components**: base-surface, card, glass-surface
- **Key features**:
  - `TxGlassSurface` draws its displacement map as a bitmap at most 256px on its long side and stretches it. Chromium rasterizes the map on the CPU for every frame; the full-size map cost a large panel 100–200ms a frame, the bitmap under 1ms.
  - `refraction` uses the `css` renderer by default and draws no SVG glass layer. Pass `refractionRenderer="svg"` where the refraction should show, and set its strength with the new `refractionGlassOpacity` (`0.3` by default). `TxCard` forwards both props.
  - `setSurfacePerformanceMode('max')` gives every costly material on the page a solid fill, except on `systemBackdrop` surfaces.
  - `TxCard`'s SVG glass layer no longer disappears when a host clips the card with `overflow: hidden` or nests it in a rounded clipping container.

### Version 0.9.0 (2026-10-20)

Learning curves, gesture interactions and refraction surfaces, including the previously unreleased component changes.

- **New components**: No new standalone component modules; the learning curve is exported from `charts`.
- **Main updated components**: alert, allocation-bar, attachment-tray, base-surface, card-spread, carousel-3d, charts, command-palette, dialog, drawer, fine-tune-card, flip-book, image-gallery, markdown-editor, modal, motion-dock, physics-motion, stream-element, stream-markdown, stream-text, thinking-orb, toast
- **Key features**:
  - `TxLearningCurve` supports smoothing, multi-seed bands and viewport windows. Charts add press-to-read, zoom, pan and keyboard controls; the learning curve's Y-axis name no longer overlaps its ticks.
  - Carousel, flip book, card spread and physics motion support direct dragging and momentum release; Motion Dock updates its surface and magnification layout.
  - Modal, Drawer, Command Palette and dialogs use refraction surfaces; transparent windows can enable `systemBackdrop`.
  - Markdown Editor supports block editing, lazy-loaded CodeMirror, image uploads, AI rewrites, comments and collaboration interfaces.
  - Attachment Tray and Image Gallery share a previewer with focus restoration, failure states and accessible icon-button labels; Thinking Orb adds gradient palettes.

### Version 0.8.0 (2026-10-14)

Fixed brand-color surface lighting, voice-message playback, semantic data tables and form sizing fixes.

- **New components (2)**: [flow-light](/en/flow-light), [voice-clip](/en/voice-clip)
- **Updated components (13)**: base-anchor, base-surface, button, card, conversation-stream, data-table, dropdown-menu, input, number-input, select, tag-input, textarea, voice-beam
- **Key features**:
  - `TxFlowLight` supports corners / rim / aurora, with fixed brand-color lighting forwarded by BaseSurface, Card and menu panels; hidden in high-contrast mode
  - `TxVoiceClip` provides playback, waveform seeking, keyboard controls, local recording decoding and one-at-a-time playback; `TxVoiceBeam` adds independent `organic` motion and respects reduced-motion preferences
  - `TxButton` adds `progress`, `showProgress` and `formatProgress`; `TxConversationStream` measures restored conversation rows on mount
  - `TxDataTable` adds semantic column `type`, per-column `filter` / `filterOptions`, controlled `filter` / `defaultFilter`, and `update:filter` / `filterChange`. Client-side filtering is on by default; `filterOnClient=false` delegates filtering to the caller, and `autoStickyActions` fixes action columns to the right by default
  - `TxSelect` enables search at `searchThreshold` options (8 by default) when `searchable` is omitted; explicit `false` or a nonpositive threshold disables automatic search
  - Input, Textarea, Select, NumberInput and TagInput explicitly use `border-box`, without relying on a host reset or injecting a global wildcard reset
  - After extracting DataTable data state and deduplicating its styles, component JS is 42.9 KiB and full / on-demand CSS is 749.0 / 719.6 KiB; aggregate baselines are 750 / 720.5 KiB, with per-file budgets and import restrictions unchanged


